1
00:04:07,199 --> 00:04:13,199
Alone in Berlin is a war, thriller, drama film directed by Vincent Perez.

2
00:08:14,399 --> 00:08:20,399
Berlin in June of 1940.

3
00:12:21,599 --> 00:12:27,599
While Nazi propaganda celebrates the regime’s victory over France, a
kitchen-cum-living room in Prenzlauer Berg is filled with grief.

4
00:16:28,799 --> 00:16:34,799
Anna and Otto Quangel’s son has been killed at the front.

5
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:42,000
This working class couple had long believed in the ‘Führer’ and followed him willingly,
but now they realise that his promises are nothing but lies and deceit.

6
00:24:43,199 --> 00:24:49,199
They begin writing postcards as a form of resistance and in a
bid to raise awareness: Stop the war machine!

7
00:28:50,399 --> 00:28:56,399
Kill Hitler!

8
00:32:57,599 --> 00:33:03,599
Putting their lives at risk, they distribute these cards in the
entrances of tenement buildings and in stairwells.

9
00:37:04,799 --> 00:37:10,799
But the SS and the Gestapo are soon onto them, and
even their neighbours pose a threat.

10
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:18,000
Anna Quangel, played by Emma Thompson.

11
00:45:19,199 --> 00:45:25,199
Otto Quangel, played by Brendan Gleeson.

12
00:49:26,399 --> 00:49:32,399
Escherich, played by Daniel Brühl.

13
00:53:33,599 --> 00:53:39,599
Prall, played by Mikael Persbrandt.

14
00:57:40,799 --> 00:57:46,799
Claire Gehrich, played by Katharina Schüttler.

15
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:54,000
Hans Quangel, played by Louis Hofmann.

16
01:05:55,199 --> 01:06:01,199
Alone in Berlin is a 2016 war drama film which was directed by
Vincent Pérez and written by Pérez and Achim von Borries.

17
01:10:02,399 --> 01:10:08,399
It is based on the 1947 novel Every Man Dies Alone, by Hans Fallada.

18
01:14:09,599 --> 01:14:15,599
The novel's characters Otto and Anna Quangel are based on Otto and Elise Hampel.

19
01:18:16,800 --> 01:18:22,800
When their son dies in France, the couple start writing postcards to urge
people to protest against Adolf Hitler and the Nazi regime.

20
01:22:24,000 --> 01:22:30,000
The film stars Emma Thompson, Brendan Gleeson,
Daniel Brühl, and Mikael Persbrandt.

21
01:26:31,199 --> 01:26:37,199
Principal photography began on 27 March 2015 in Berlin.

22
01:30:38,399 --> 01:30:44,399
It was selected to compete for the Golden Bear at the
66th Berlin International Film Festival.

23
01:34:45,599 --> 01:34:51,599
The film explores themes of berlin, germany, based on
novel or book, world war ii, 1940s.

24
01:38:52,799 --> 01:38:58,799
The tone is emotional and intense.
